<context>
Epic EP-001 — Calendar clones through Calendar.app.
Goal: every calendar the Operator owns shows the busy slots of the other calendars, so colleagues on any account
see the real availability and the Operator gets notified on every client.
Architecture: a single Swift executable (`calsyn-cli`, Swift Package `calsyn`) talks to the calendar store
through EventKit and never touches credentials. The `reconciler` is pure logic over the `calendar-store`
abstraction, so it is tested against an in-memory fake.

Scope of this workflow:
- TASK-003: for each job, `calsyn once` makes every destination hold exactly one clone per source event in the
  window (today → +7 days), creating the missing clones and deleting the extra ones.
  Components: reconciler, calendar-store, runner.
- TASK-005: `window.past_days` and `window.future_days` in the config change the window, and nothing outside it
  is ever created or deleted. Components: config-loader, reconciler.
</context>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-003.md</input>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-005.md</input>
<coding_test>
- `swift test`: reconciler on the in-memory fake store (AS-04..AS-08, AS-18); run on every change.
- `swift test`: window boundaries and override on the fake store (AS-11); run on every change.
- Manual E2E: `calsyn once` on a Mac with Exchange + Google, check both calendars in Calendar.app (AS-04, AS-05); before closing TASK-003.
</coding_test>
<available_agents>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:developer" id="developer">Implements the code of the tasks and applies the fixes requested by the reviewer.</agent>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:devils-advocate" id="devils-advocate">Reviews the implementation against the tasks' Definition of Done and the epic's architecture, and reports the gaps to the developer.</agent>
</available_agents>
<tasks>
    <task id="task-003">
        `developer` implements TASK-003. Definition of Done:
        - A source event with no clone yet → after `calsyn once` each destination shows an event titled `&lt;prefix&gt;` with the same start and end
        - With `details.title: true` the clone is titled `&lt;prefix&gt; &lt;title&gt;`; with `details.description: true` the clone notes show the source description
        - A source event moved, or with a cloned field changed → after the reconcile the destination shows only the updated clone
        - A source event deleted → after the reconcile its clone is gone from the destination
        - Events whose title starts with any configured `clone_prefix` are never cloned: with jobs A→B and B→A, the second consecutive `calsyn once` logs `created=0 deleted=0` for both jobs
        - Clones left by the old system that match a wanted clone stay; the others are deleted
        - Each job logs one INFO summary line with `created=N deleted=N`
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="task-005">
        `developer` implements TASK-005. Definition of Done:
        - Without `window` in the config, only events from the start of today to +7 days are cloned
        - With `window.past_days` / `window.future_days` set, the clones cover exactly that range
        - Source events and clones outside the window are neither created nor deleted
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="close-specs">
        Rename `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-003.md` to `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-003-done.md` and
        `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-005.md` to `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-005-done.md`.
        Update every reference to the old names under `alligator/specs/`.
    </task>
</tasks>
